# Phaser Component Architecture Foundation

## Context
- When creating complex Phaser game entities with multiple behaviors
- When code reuse across different entity types is important in a Phaser game
- When entity behavior needs to be modified at runtime
- When working on medium to large Phaser game projects

## Requirements
- Use Phaser.GameObjects as the foundation for component-based entity design
- Create a robust entity-component framework that integrates with Phaser's lifecycle
- Implement proper component management within entities
- Ensure clean resource management and event cleanup in components
- Design components to be self-contained and focused on a single responsibility

## Examples

```typescript
// Component interface compatible with Phaser's lifecycle
interface Component {
  init?(): void;
  preUpdate?(time: number, delta: number): void;
  update(time: number, delta: number): void;
  postUpdate?(time: number, delta: number): void;
  destroy(): void;
}

// Base entity class that integrates with Phaser's GameObject system
class PhaserEntity extends Phaser.GameObjects.Container {
  private components: Map<string, Component> = new Map();
  private registeredEvents: { target: Phaser.Events.EventEmitter, event: string, fn: Function, context: any }[] = [];

  constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene, x: number, y: number) {
    super(scene, x, y);
    // Add to scene and update list
    scene.add.existing(this);
    scene.sys.updateList.add(this);
  }

  // Add component and initialize it
  addComponent<T extends Component>(name: string, component: T): T {
    this.components.set(name, component);
    
    // Call initialization if it exists
    if (component.init) {
      component.init();
    }
    
    return component;
  }

  // Get component by name with proper TypeScript typing
  getComponent<T extends Component>(name: string): T | undefined {
    return this.components.get(name) as T;
  }

  // Check if component exists
  hasComponent(name: string): boolean {
    return this.components.has(name);
  }

  // Remove component and clean it up
  removeComponent(name: string): boolean {
    const component = this.components.get(name);
    if (component) {
      component.destroy();
      return this.components.delete(name);
    }
    return false;
  }

  // Register event for automatic cleanup
  addEvent(target: Phaser.Events.EventEmitter, event: string, fn: Function, context: any): void {
    target.on(event, fn, context);
    this.registeredEvents.push({ target, event, fn, context });
  }

  // Phaser lifecycle methods
  preUpdate(time: number, delta: number): void {
    // Call preUpdate on all components that implement it
    this.components.forEach(component => {
      if (component.preUpdate) {
        component.preUpdate(time, delta);
      }
    });
  }

  update(time: number, delta: number): void {
    // Update all components
    this.components.forEach(component => component.update(time, delta));
  }

  postUpdate(time: number, delta: number): void {
    // Call postUpdate on all components that implement it
    this.components.forEach(component => {
      if (component.postUpdate) {
        component.postUpdate(time, delta);
      }
    });
  }

  destroy(fromScene?: boolean): void {
    // Clean up all components
    this.components.forEach(component => component.destroy());
    this.components.clear();
    
    // Remove all registered event listeners
    this.registeredEvents.forEach(({ target, event, fn, context }) => {
      target.off(event, fn, context);
    });
    this.registeredEvents = [];
    
    // Call parent destroy method
    super.destroy(fromScene);
  }
}
```

## Implementation Approaches

### Container-Based Composition

Using Phaser's Container as a base class provides the best flexibility for component-based entities:

```typescript
// The container holds visual elements and components
const enemy = new PhaserEntity(scene, x, y);
const sprite = scene.add.sprite(0, 0, 'enemy');
enemy.add(sprite);

// Adding components that can work with any container-based entity
enemy.addComponent('health', new HealthComponent(enemy, 100));
enemy.addComponent('movement', new MovementComponent(enemy, 150));
```

### Extended GameObject Approach

For simpler entities, extending Phaser GameObjects and adding component functionality:

```typescript
class ComponentGameObject extends Phaser.GameObjects.Sprite {
  private components: Map<string, Component> = new Map();
  
  // Component methods...
  
  update(time: number, delta: number): void {
    // Update components
    this.components.forEach(component => component.update(time, delta));
  }
}
```

### Proper Event Handling

Always clean up event listeners to prevent memory leaks:

```typescript
// In your component or entity class
private events: Array<{emitter: Phaser.Events.EventEmitter, event: string, listener: Function}> = [];

// Register event with tracking
addEvent(emitter: Phaser.Events.EventEmitter, event: string, listener: Function): void {
  emitter.on(event, listener, this);
  this.events.push({ emitter, event, listener });
}

// Cleanup on destroy
destroy(): void {
  this.events.forEach(({ emitter, event, listener }) => {
    emitter.off(event, listener, this);
  });
  this.events = [];
}
```

